//? Title: Ellipsoid Cuts: Geometry, Actual Oracles and Honest Stopping
//? Subtitle: Positive triangular factors, conditional objective bounds and measured volume shrinkage
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
A convex subgradient determines a halfspace that retains a minimizer.
The ellipsoid method encloses that half of the current ellipsoid in a
new ellipsoid. We begin with a unit circle, derive the exact change in
volume, and inspect the actual callback trajectory of the original
weighted quadratic. Native C++ datamunge APIs keep the geometry in a
positive triangular factor and distinguish an objective tolerance from
an iteration limit or a rounded, stationary center. Shrinking volume
alone does not imply that every axis or every center objective shrinks.
)

\toc

> A unit circle and one central cut

Take c=(0,0), radius one and direction g=(1,0). The kept half is x<=0.
Its enclosing ellipse has center (-1/3,0), horizontal radius 2/3 and
vertical radius 2/sqrt(3). Its area ratio is 4/(3 sqrt(3)), about 0.7698.
The vertical axis grows even on this first step. The diagram reads the
actual geometry returned by the core; it does not implement another
cut formula in the report.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/ellipsoid_tiny.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main(){
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  const auto e=dm::algorithms::ellipsoid_ball({0,0},1);
  const auto cut=dm::algorithms::ellipsoid_central_cut(e,{1,0});
  std::print("Unit cut: center ({:.9f},{:.9f}); radii {:.9f}, {:.9f}; support {:.9f}.\n",cut.state.center[0],cut.state.center[1],cut.state.lower[0][0],cut.state.lower[1][1],cut.support_bound);
  std::print("Measured area ratio {:.12f}; exact ratio {:.12f}.\n",std::exp(cut.log_volume_after-cut.log_volume_before),4/(3*std::sqrt(3.)));
  dm::graphics::Diagram g(220,1100);
  dm::graphics::DiagramStroke old;old.color={148,163,184};old.width=3;
  dm::graphics::DiagramStroke next;next.color={37,99,235};next.width=3;
  dm::graphics::DiagramStroke axis;axis.dashed=true;axis.color={71,85,105};
  dm::graphics::DiagramStroke arrow;arrow.arrow=true;arrow.color={220,38,38};
  g.path(dm::algorithms::ellipsoid_outline(e),old).path(dm::algorithms::ellipsoid_outline(cut.state),next)
   .path({{0,-1.4},{0,1.4}},axis).path({{0,0},{.75,0}},arrow)
   .label({-.55,0},"kept x <= 0",21).text({.8,.35},"g points right",21)
   .text({-.33,-1.6},"Blue enclosing ellipse; gray original circle",22)
   .text({-.33,1.85},"One central cut retains the left half",26).save_svg("build/ellipsoid_tiny.svg");
}
```
// result_begin: markdown
