> Exact volume shrinkage does not shrink every axis

The n-dimensional volume is beta[n] det(L), where
beta[n]=pi^(n/2)/Gamma(n/2+1). Thus its log volume is
log(beta[n])+sum log(L[i,i]), computed without a determinant product.
For n>1, the exact central-cut ratio and its stable logarithm are

\[
\rho_n=\left(\frac{n^2}{n^2-1}\right)^{n/2}
\sqrt{\frac{n-1}{n+1}},\qquad
\log\rho_n=-\sum_{k\ge1}\frac{n^{-(2k-1)}}{2k(2k-1)}
\le-\frac1{2n}.
\]

The often quoted exp(-1/(2n)) is an upper bound, not the exact factor.
In one dimension rho[1]=1/2. Repeated pure geometric cuts in direction
e1 multiply the parallel radius by n/(n+1) and a perpendicular radius
by n/sqrt(n^2-1)>1. These are geometry experiments, with no claim that
a linear objective has an unconstrained minimizer. The n=2 plot checks
both actual radii and actual log-volume differences at each step.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/ellipsoid_volume.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main(){
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  std::print("| dimension | exact ratio | exp(-1/(2n)) bound |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
  for(std::size_t n:{1,2,3,5})std::print("| {} | {:.12f} | {:.12f} |\n",n,std::exp(dm::algorithms::ellipsoid_log_volume_ratio(n)),std::exp(-1/(2.*n)));
  auto e=dm::algorithms::ellipsoid_ball({0,0},1);const auto initial=dm::algorithms::ellipsoid_log_volume(e);
  std::vector<double> x,parallel,perpendicular,measured,expected;double error=0;
  for(int t=0;t<=20;++t){x.push_back(t);parallel.push_back(std::log(e.lower[0][0]));perpendicular.push_back(std::log(e.lower[1][1]));measured.push_back(dm::algorithms::ellipsoid_log_volume(e)-initial);expected.push_back(t*dm::algorithms::ellipsoid_log_volume_ratio(2));error=std::max(error,std::abs(measured.back()-expected.back()));if(t<20)e=dm::algorithms::ellipsoid_central_cut(e,{1,0}).state;}
  std::print("\nTwenty pure cuts: parallel radius {:.12g}; perpendicular radius {:.12g}; log-volume {:.12g}; maximum formula error {:.3g}.\n",e.lower[0][0],e.lower[1][1],measured.back(),error);
  auto a=dm::graphics::RPlot::create();a.line(x,parallel,"parallel",{37,99,235}).line(x,perpendicular,"perpendicular",{220,38,38}).title("One radius shrinks; another grows").x_label("Pure central cuts").y_label("Natural log(radius / initial)");
  auto b=dm::graphics::RPlot::create();b.line(x,expected,"exact formula",{220,38,38}).points(x,measured,"actual factor",{37,99,235},4).title("Volume nevertheless shrinks").x_label("Pure central cuts").y_label("Natural log(volume / initial)");
  dm::graphics::RLayout::create(1,2).add(a).add(b).size(1100,520).title("Exact central-cut geometry: volume is not the largest radius").fit_panels().save_svg("build/ellipsoid_volume.svg");
}
```
